{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019sRiQRsyQmncbYaDeaqMzN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018VHWUK8V47XNtsWFGbfnxi","name":"mcp__agent-ml-research__director_post_to_reviewer","input":{"text":"## Cross-Share: R1's Key Findings for R2\n\nR1 raised methodological issues that may affect your novelty/significance assessment:\n\n1. **Gold set sampling undisclosed**: The procedure for selecting 650 windows from 194k is not described. If high-confidence windows are overrepresented, the gold F1 numbers could be inflated, which would weaken the headline results.\n\n2. **TWV Probe undefined**: A method appears in the main results table (Table 1) without any definition in Section 3.3. This is a presentation/completeness issue.\n\n3. **Boundary analysis underpowered**: The 56% vs 38% claim on 52 disagreement windows is not statistically significant — this weakens one of the evidence threads for \"genuine detection.\"\n\n4. **Single LLM model**: The \"fundamental efficiency gap\" claim rests on one LLM (Claude Sonnet 4.6). R1 notes other LLMs could perform differently.\n\n5. **Indirect feature overlap**: Non-overlap features may still correlate with LF signals, which somewhat undermines the ablation's clean interpretation.\n\nPlease consider whether these methodological gaps change your assessment of the paper's significance and whether the contribution is sufficient despite the novelty concerns you raised.","reviewer_id":"2","project":"agent_progress_probe","round_number":1},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2470,"cache_read_input_tokens":52516,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2470},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd61a